The current six-step workflow and rebuild checklist are in [WORKFLOW.md](WORKFLOW.md) and [research/workflow-rebuild-plan.md](research/workflow-rebuild-plan.md).

Algorithms (`alg-`) are definition-like procedures; see [SCHEMA.md](SCHEMA.md#algorithms).

The [2026-10-11 published-only scaffold audits](research/scaffold-audit-2026-10-11/README.md) update classical mechanics, quantum mechanics, general relativity and thermodynamics. Their external mathematics uses published canonical suppliers; draft EM/SR physics is permitted only at its actual inspected scope. The later [owner-directed GR repair](research/gr-repair-2026-10-11/report.md) closes the three GR proof holds with local arguments for smooth splitting, generic dust evolution and MGHD gluing; source and production-acceptance limits remain recorded. These are research dispositions, not production readiness.

The [2026-10-12 scaffold audits](research/scaffold-audit-2026-10-12/README.md) repair Thermodynamics, Relativistic Particle Mechanics and QFT, with inspected actual draft suppliers permitted. Statistics and Numerical Analysis scaffolds are excluded from all supplier chains. Current receipts distinguish authored items, local research arguments, physical assumptions and open problems; they do not confer production acceptance.

