research/advanced-qft-supersymmetry-2026-10-23/research-supersymmetry.md:696:## Source ledger and dated reading limits
research/advanced-qft-supersymmetry-2026-10-23/research-supersymmetry.md:706:| Rudolf Haag, Jan T. Łopuszański, Martin Sohnius, “All Possible Generators of Supersymmetries of the S-Matrix,” *Nucl. Phys. B* 88 (1975) 257–274, DOI <https://doi.org/10.1016/0550-3213(75)90279-5>; full-text university mirror <https://www.physics.mcgill.ca/~keshav/675/haag.pdf> | Full 18-page mirror retrieved; read abstract, §1, assumptions in §2, and the massive-algebra classification in §3. | The theorem concerns visible S-matrix symmetries, a nontrivial S-matrix, particle finiteness, and a massive theory without massless particles/long-range forces; authors explicitly limit massless classification because of infrared/vacuum-degeneracy issues. This is not a blanket theorem for arbitrary local QFT or a proof that nature is supersymmetric. |
research/advanced-qft-supersymmetry-2026-10-23/research-supersymmetry.md:709:| N. Seiberg and E. Witten, “Monopole Condensation, and Confinement in N=2 Supersymmetric Yang-Mills Theory,” arXiv:hep-th/9407087v1 (15 Jul 1994), <https://arxiv.org/pdf/hep-th/9407087v1> | Full 45-page PDF retrieved; read §§1–2.3, §§3–4, §§5.1–5.7 and §6. | Pure \(SU(2)\), N=2, low-energy curve/prepotential, periods, BPS mass formula, monodromy, and proposed massless monopole/dyon singularities. The source calls its singularity input a proposal and works inside a physical low-energy effective-action framework; it does not construct the ultraviolet continuum path integral. |
research/advanced-qft-supersymmetry-2026-10-23/research-supersymmetry.md:710:| N. Seiberg, “Electric-Magnetic Duality in Supersymmetric Non-Abelian Gauge Theories,” arXiv:hep-th/9411149v1 (20 Nov 1994), <https://arxiv.org/pdf/hep-th/9411149v1> | Full 22-page PDF retrieved; read §1, the SQCD conformal-window discussion in §§2–3, and deformation/anomaly checks in §§4–5. | Primary source for the electric/magnetic SQCD proposal. It explicitly says “we cannot prove” the proposed fixed point for every value in the window and presents the dual variables as a suggested description checked against anomalies and deformations. This is not a local proof of equivalence. |
research/advanced-qft-supersymmetry-2026-10-23/research-supersymmetry.md:711:| K. Intriligator and N. Seiberg, “Lectures on Supersymmetric Gauge Theories and Electric-Magnetic Duality,” arXiv:hep-th/9509066v1 (12 Sep 1995), <https://arxiv.org/pdf/hep-th/9509066v1> | Full 44-page PDF retrieved; read §§1.1–1.3, §§2.1–2.4, and §§5.1–5.3. | Review source for moduli, holomorphy, the conformal window, and dual SQCD description. Its phrasing identifies an equivalent infrared description in theoretical physics; it does not supply a constructive mathematical equivalence proof. |
research/advanced-qft-supersymmetry-2026-10-23/research-supersymmetry.md:712:| N. Seiberg, “Naturalness Versus Supersymmetric Non-renormalization Theorems,” arXiv:hep-ph/9309335v1 (30 Sep 1993), <https://arxiv.org/pdf/hep-ph/9309335v1>; “The Power of Holomorphy,” arXiv:hep-th/9408013v1, <https://arxiv.org/pdf/hep-th/9408013v1> | Full 14-page and 13-page PDFs retrieved; read Seiberg 1993 §§1–4 and 1994 §§1–2.2. | Supports the perturbative/nonperturbative and Wilsonian/1PI distinction. The 1993 argument explicitly assumes the theories exist as quantum field theories and that regularization preserves SUSY/global symmetries; it identifies nonperturbative superpotential corrections and IR holomorphic anomalies in 1PI. |
research/advanced-qft-supersymmetry-2026-10-23/research-supersymmetry.md:715:| Caetano, Komatsu, Soresina, Wallberg, “Orientifold and Integrability: N=4 Super-Yang-Mills on RP4,” arXiv:2610.28725v1 (20 Oct 2026), <https://arxiv.org/pdf/2610.28725> | Full preprint retrieved; read abstract/introduction, the localization section setup, and conclusion; the lengthy spin-chain and localization calculations were not independently reproduced. | Recent research lead concerning planar N=4 SYM on \(\mathbb{RP}^4\), with a conjectured general formula and evidence for a holographic orientifold interpretation. It is not a proof of S-duality or a general localization theorem. |
