        "inventory_expansion_required": true,
        "statement": "Let $X$ be a Hausdorff, second-countable smooth manifold covered by open sets $U$ and $V$. Let $G$ be a finite-dimensional, Hausdorff, second-countable real Lie group, and let $\\tau:U\\cap V\\to G$ be smooth. On the disjoint union $Q=(U\\times G)_U\\sqcup(V\\times G)_V$, impose the equivalence relation generated, for $x\\in U\\cap V$ and $h\\in G$, by\n\n$$ (x,h)_V\\sim (x,\\tau(x)h)_U. $$\n\nLet $P:=Q/{\\sim}$ with the quotient topology, write $[x,h]_U$ and $[x,h]_V$ for its classes, and define $\\pi:P\\to X$ by $\\pi([x,h]_U)=\\pi([x,h]_V)=x$. Define the right action by $[x,h]_i\\cdot k=[x,hk]_i$ for $k\\in G$ and $i\\in\\{U,V\\}$. Then $P$ is a smooth right principal $G$-bundle over $X$. Its local sections $s_U(x)=[x,e]_U$ and $s_V(x)=[x,e]_V$ satisfy $s_V(x)=s_U(x)\\tau(x)$ on $U\\cap V$.",
