        "inventory_expansion_required": false,
        "statement": "Assume full Axiom of Choice. Let $X$ be a nonempty, connected, compact, oriented, finite-dimensional Hausdorff second-countable smooth four-manifold without boundary, with a supplied Riemannian metric. Let $G\\subseteq U(V,h)$ be a compact non-Abelian matrix Lie group in its specified global form, let $\\pi:P\\to X$ be a smooth right principal $G$-bundle in a specified bundle sector (an isomorphism class of smooth principal bundles under isomorphisms over $X$), and let $\\omega$ be a supplied smooth principal connection. Let $B:\\mathfrak g\\times\\mathfrak g\\to\\mathbb R$ be a positive-definite symmetric bilinear form invariant under $\\operatorname{Ad}(G)$. For local sections $s_i:U_i\\to P$, set $A_i=s_i^*\\omega$ and $F_i=dA_i+\\tfrac12[A_i\\wedge A_i]$. If $F_i=\\sum_a e_a F_i^a$ in a finite basis of $\\mathfrak g$, define $B(F_i\\wedge F_i):=\\sum_{a,b}B(e_a,e_b)F_i^a\\wedge F_i^b$; this expression is independent of the basis. Invariance of $B$ makes the local expressions $\\beta_B|_{U_i}:=(8\\pi^2)^{-1}B(F_i\\wedge F_i)$ restrictions of a global four-form $\\beta_B$. The **trace-normalized topological charge** is\n\n$$\nq_B(P,\\omega):=\\int_X\\beta_B.\n$$\n\nThe number $q_B(P,\\omega)$ is independent of the supplied connection. For a general compact matrix group and invariant $B$, it is a real characteristic number; no integrality is asserted. In the special case $G=SU(2)$ in its defining representation on $\\mathbb C^2$, with $h(v,w)=v^*w$ and $B(X,Y)=-\\operatorname{tr}_2(XY)$, the associated Hermitian bundle $E=P\\times_{SU(2)}\\mathbb C^2$ has\n\n$$\nq_B(P,\\omega)=-\\langle c_2(E),[X]\\rangle\\in\\mathbb Z,\n$$\n\nwhere $c_2(E)\\in H^4(X;\\mathbb Z)$ is the integral second Chern class and $[X]\\in H_4(X;\\mathbb Z)$ is the orientation fundamental class. This sign is fixed by the library convention $c(E,\\nabla)=\\det(I-\\Omega_\\nabla/(2\\pi i))$.\n\nThe Hodge operator $*_g$ on two-forms is characterized by $\\alpha\\wedge *_g\\beta=\\langle\\alpha,\\beta\\rangle_g\\,d\\operatorname{vol}_g$ and acts componentwise on $\\mathfrak g$-valued forms. Set $F_i^+=(F_i+*_gF_i)/2$ and $F_i^-=(F_i-*_gF_i)/2$. The self-dual sector consists of connections with $F_i^-=0$, equivalently $F_i=*_gF_i$; the anti-self-dual (ASD) sector consists of connections with $F_i^+=0$, equivalently $F_i=-*_gF_i$. These conditions are independent of the local section.",
