        "statement": "Assume the Axiom of Countable Choice. Use the four-dimensional rigid N=2 super-Poincare convention with metric $\\eta=\\operatorname{diag}(-1,1,1,1)$, $\\epsilon_{12}=1$, and natural units $\\hbar=c=1$. Let $\\mathcal K\\ne\\{0\\}$ be a positive Hilbert rest-fiber representation with $P^\\mu=(M,0,0,0)$, $M>0$, scalar central charges $Z^{12}=zI$ and $Z^{21}=-zI$, and a common dense invariant domain $\\mathcal D$ on which the supercharges, their actual Hilbert adjoints, and every product below are defined. Thus $P_0=-M$, each supercharge has mass dimension one-half, and $M,z$ have mass dimension one. Choose $\\phi\\in\\mathbb R$ so that $e^{-i\\phi}z=|z|$, with arbitrary $\\phi$ when $z=0$, and on $\\mathcal D$ put\n\n$$q=Q^1_1,\\qquad r=Q^2_2,\\qquad A=q-e^{i\\phi}r^*,\\qquad A^\\sharp=q^*-e^{-i\\phi}r.$$\n\nFor every $\\psi\\in\\mathcal D$,\n\n$$\\langle(AA^\\sharp+A^\\sharp A)\\psi,\\psi\\rangle=\\|A\\psi\\|^2+\\|A^\\sharp\\psi\\|^2=4(M-|z|)\\|\\psi\\|^2.$$\n\nConsequently, for every nonzero $\\psi\\in\\mathcal D$, $M=|z|$ if and only if $A\\psi=A^\\sharp\\psi=0$. The operator $A^\\sharp$ is the displayed sum of the individual charge adjoints; for unbounded charges it is not asserted to be the maximal-domain adjoint of the sum $A$. This conditional statement neither asserts that such a vector or representation occurs in a physical model nor proves its dynamical stability.",
